IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr2-helpers`

-- PART 5 -- BENEFICIAL OWNERSHIP INFORMATION: APPLICATION, CORPORATE BODIES AND TRUSTEES (regulations 42 to 44) of the Money
-- Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 (S.I. 2017/692), United
-- Kingdom.  Lines 1320-1414 of the text.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- LAYER 1: THE LAW, OBJECTIVELY.  A rule answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (a MAYBE BOOLEAN):
-- JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING where it does not answer.
--
-- INPUTS THAT ANOTHER SECTION ANSWERS (seams, see NOTES.md "Seams (mlr2)"):
--   S-1   `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures`   (regulation 27, part mlr1)
--   S-8   `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`                                             (regulation 8, part mlr1)
--   S-18  `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`                                 (Schedule 3A, part mlr5)
--   S-K1  `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`                                   (regulation 4, keel)
--   S-K2  `reg 5 and 6 any person qualifies as a beneficial owner of the body corporate`       (regulations 5 and 6, keel)
-- Three dates are not in the rendering (lines 1333, 1513, 1516: "the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force").  They are
-- inputs of type DATE and are never guessed.

§ `Part 5 -- Beneficial ownership information (regulations 42 to 44)`

§§ `Regulation 42 -- Application of this Part`

-- reg 42(2)(a): a UK body corporate.  The paragraph says "is a body corporate which is incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom", and "includes" adds only the eligible Scottish partnership: a body that is neither is not one.
-- src:1323 | (2) For the purposes of this Part—
@ref reg 42(2) (src:1323-1323)
-- src:1324 | (a) a “UK body corporate” is a body corporate which is incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of the United Kingdom, and includes an eligible Scottish partnership;
@ref reg 42(2)(a) (src:1324-1324)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate which is incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is an eligible Scottish partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the body is a body corporate which is incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of the United Kingdom` OR `the body is an eligible Scottish partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'UK body corporate' is a body corporate which is incorporated under the law of the United Kingdom or any part of the United Kingdom"; "includes" adds only the eligible Scottish partnership, so a company incorporated elsewhere (a Jersey company, say) is not one

-- reg 42(3): a trustee or settlor is resident in the United Kingdom.
DECLARE `reg 42(3) kind of trustee or settlor` IS ONE OF
    `reg 42(3)(a) a body corporate`
    `reg 42(3)(b) an individual`

-- src:1346 | (3) A trustee or settlor is resident in the United Kingdom—
-- src:1347 | (a) in the case of a body corporate, if it is a UK body corporate;
-- src:1348 | (b) in the case of an individual, if the individual is resident in the United Kingdom for the purposes of one or more of the taxes referred to in regulation 45(14).
@ref reg 42(3) (src:1346-1348)
GIVEN kind IS A `reg 42(3) kind of trustee or settlor`
      `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is resident in the United Kingdom for the purposes of one or more of the taxes referred to in regulation 45(14)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(3) the trustee or settlor is resident in the United Kingdom` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `reg 42(3)(a) a body corporate` THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a body corporate, if it is a UK body corporate" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a UK body corporate has not been answered
    WHEN `reg 42(3)(b) an individual` THEN
        IF `the individual is resident in the United Kingdom for the purposes of one or more of the taxes referred to in regulation 45(14)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an individual, if the individual is resident in the United Kingdom for the purposes of one or more of the taxes" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 42(2)(d) with 42(2A): the settlor's residence.  For a trust set up before 6 April 2025 the settlor must have been resident AND domiciled.
DECLARE `reg 42(2)(d) the facts` HAS
    `at least one trustee is resident in the United Kingdom`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the settlor was resident in the United Kingdom when the trust was set up`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the settlor was domiciled in the United Kingdom when the trust was set up`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the settlor was resident in the United Kingdom when the settlor added funds to the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the settlor was domiciled in the United Kingdom when the settlor added funds to the trust` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1338 | (d) this sub-paragraph applies if—
-- src:1339 | (i) at least one trustee is resident in the United Kingdom, and
-- src:1340 | (ii) the settlor was resident ... in the United Kingdom at the time when—
-- src:1341 | (aa) the trust was set up, or
-- src:1342 | (bb) the settlor added funds to the trust;
@ref reg 42(2)(d) (src:1338-1342)
-- src:1345 | (2A) In relation to a trust that was set up before 6 April 2025, paragraph (2)(d)(ii) has effect as if after “resident” there were inserted “and domiciled”.
@ref reg 42(2A) (src:1345-1345)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(d) the facts`
      `the date on which the trust was set up` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(2)(d) sub-paragraph (d) applies` MEANS
    IF facts's `at least one trustee is resident in the United Kingdom` AND (`at the time the trust was set up` OR `at the time the settlor added funds`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this sub-paragraph applies if (i) at least one trustee is resident in the United Kingdom, and (ii) the settlor was resident ... at the time when ..." (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)
    WHERE
        -- regulation 42(2A): for a trust "set up before 6 April 2025", "resident" reads "resident and domiciled"
        `the version with domicile applies` MEANS `the date on which the trust was set up` LESS THAN Date 6 4 2025
        `at the time the trust was set up` MEANS
            facts's `the settlor was resident in the United Kingdom when the trust was set up`
            AND (IF `the version with domicile applies` THEN facts's `the settlor was domiciled in the United Kingdom when the trust was set up` ELSE TRUE)
        `at the time the settlor added funds` MEANS
            facts's `the settlor was resident in the United Kingdom when the settlor added funds to the trust`
            AND (IF `the version with domicile applies` THEN facts's `the settlor was domiciled in the United Kingdom when the settlor added funds to the trust` ELSE TRUE)

-- reg 42(2)(c) and (e): UK trust and non-UK trust.
-- src:1335 | (c) a trust is a “UK trust” if—
-- src:1336 | (i) all the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom; or
-- src:1337 | (ii) sub-paragraph (d) applies;
@ref reg 42(2)(c) (src:1335-1337)
GIVEN `all the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(d) sub-paragraph (d) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` MEANS
    IF `all the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `reg 42(2)(d) sub-paragraph (d) applies` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a trust is a 'UK trust' if (i) all the trustees are resident in the United Kingdom; or (ii) sub-paragraph (d) applies" -- sub-paragraph (d) supplies the "no" or the "not answered"

-- src:1343 | (e) a trust is a “non-UK trust” if it is not a UK trust;
@ref reg 42(2)(e) (src:1343-1343)
GIVEN `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(2)(e) the trust is a non-UK trust` MEANS
    `mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a trust is a 'non-UK trust' if it is not a UK trust"

-- reg 42(4): an EEA registered trust.
-- src:1349 | (4) For the purposes of this Part, an “EEA registered trust” is a trust established in a country or territory other than the United Kingdom where national legislation applies having a broadly equivalent effect to the requirements laid down in the fourth money laundering directive.
@ref reg 42(4) (src:1349-1349)
GIVEN `the trust is established in a country or territory other than the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `national legislation applies there having a broadly equivalent effect to the requirements laid down in the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(4) the trust is an EEA registered trust` MEANS
    IF `the trust is established in a country or territory other than the United Kingdom` AND `national legislation applies there having a broadly equivalent effect to the requirements laid down in the fourth money laundering directive`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an 'EEA registered trust' is a trust established in a country or territory other than the United Kingdom where national legislation applies having a broadly equivalent effect"

-- reg 42(5): the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom.
DECLARE `reg 42(5) registration` IS ONE OF
    `reg 42(5)(a)(i) registered in the register of title kept under the Land Registration Act 2002 as the proprietor of a freehold estate in land`
    `reg 42(5)(a)(ii) registered in the register of title kept under the Land Registration Act 2002 as the proprietor of a leasehold estate in land granted for a term of more than 7 years`
    `reg 42(5)(b) registered in the Land Register of Scotland as the proprietor`
    `reg 42(5)(b) registered in the Land Register of Scotland as the tenant under a lease`
    `reg 42(5)(c)(i) registered in the register kept under the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 as the owner of a freehold estate in land`
    `reg 42(5)(c)(ii) registered in the register kept under the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 as the owner of a leasehold estate in land granted for a term of more than 21 years`

-- src:1350 | (5) For the purposes of this Part, the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom where at least one of the trustees becomes registered—
-- src:1351 | (a) in the register of title kept under the Land Registration Act 2002 as the proprietor of—
-- src:1352 | (i) a freehold estate in land; or
-- src:1353 | (ii) a leasehold estate in land granted for a term of more than 7 years from the date of the grant;
-- src:1354 | (b) in the Land Register of Scotland as the proprietor or as the tenant under a lease (“lease” and “proprietor” having the meanings given by section 113(1) of the Land Registration etc. (Scotland) Act 2012); or
-- src:1355 | (c) in the register kept under the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 as the owner of—
-- src:1356 | (i) a freehold estate in land; or
-- src:1357 | (ii) a leasehold estate in land granted for a term of more than 21 years from the date of the grant.
@ref reg 42(5) (src:1350-1357)
GIVEN `at least one of the trustees becomes registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      registration IS A `reg 42(5) registration`
      `the term for which the leasehold estate was granted, in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(5) the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom` MEANS
    IF `at least one of the trustees becomes registered` AND `the registration is of the kind the paragraph names`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom where at least one of the trustees becomes registered ..." (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    WHERE
        `the registration is of the kind the paragraph names` MEANS
            CONSIDER registration
            WHEN `reg 42(5)(a)(i) registered in the register of title kept under the Land Registration Act 2002 as the proprietor of a freehold estate in land` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 42(5)(a)(ii) registered in the register of title kept under the Land Registration Act 2002 as the proprietor of a leasehold estate in land granted for a term of more than 7 years` THEN `the term for which the leasehold estate was granted, in years` GREATER THAN 7
            WHEN `reg 42(5)(b) registered in the Land Register of Scotland as the proprietor` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 42(5)(b) registered in the Land Register of Scotland as the tenant under a lease` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 42(5)(c)(i) registered in the register kept under the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 as the owner of a freehold estate in land` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `reg 42(5)(c)(ii) registered in the register kept under the Land Registration Act (Northern Ireland) 1970 as the owner of a leasehold estate in land granted for a term of more than 21 years` THEN `the term for which the leasehold estate was granted, in years` GREATER THAN 21

-- reg 42(6): the controlling interest in a third country entity, and the third country entity.
-- The conditions are those of paragraphs 2 to 5 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006, which is not among the sources: each is asked as a fact.
-- src:1358 | (6) For the purposes of this Part—
-- src:1359 | (a) the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity if they meet any of the specified conditions in paragraphs 2 to 5 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006 (people with significant control over a company) where that Schedule is read with the following modifications—
-- src:1360 | (i) references to X having or holding a share in or a right in relation to, or exercising significant influence or control over, company Y are to be read as references to the trustees (in their capacity as such) having or holding a share in or a right in relation to, or exercising significant influence or control over, the third country entity;
-- src:1361 | (ii) for “25%” wherever it occurs in each of paragraphs 2 (ownership of shares), 3 (voting rights), 13 (calculating shareholdings), and 14 (voting rights), read “50%”; and
@ref reg 42(6)(a) (src:1358-1361)
GIVEN `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 2 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006 (ownership of shares), read with 50% for 25%` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 3 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006 (voting rights), read with 50% for 25%` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 4 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 5 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(6)(a) the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity` MEANS
    IF `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 2 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006 (ownership of shares), read with 50% for 25%`
       OR `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 3 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006 (voting rights), read with 50% for 25%`
       OR `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 4 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006`
       OR `the trustees meet the condition in paragraph 5 of Schedule 1A to the Companies Act 2006`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the trustees have a controlling interest in a third country entity if they meet any of the specified conditions" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- src:1362 | (b) “third country entity” means a body corporate, partnership or other entity that—
-- src:1363 | (i) is governed by the law of a country or territory other than the United Kingdom and (in each case) is a legal person under that law, and
-- src:1364 | (ii) is not subject to national legislation having a broadly equivalent effect to the requirements laid down in Article 30 of the fourth money laundering directive.
@ref reg 42(6)(b) (src:1362-1364)
GIVEN `the entity is governed by the law of a country or territory other than the United Kingdom and is a legal person under that law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the entity is subject to national legislation having a broadly equivalent effect to the requirements laid down in Article 30 of the fourth money laundering directive` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(6)(b) the entity is a third country entity` MEANS
    IF `the entity is governed by the law of a country or territory other than the United Kingdom and is a legal person under that law` AND (NOT `the entity is subject to national legislation having a broadly equivalent effect to the requirements laid down in Article 30 of the fourth money laundering directive`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'third country entity' means a body corporate, partnership or other entity that"

-- reg 42(2)(f): a pointer.
-- src:1344 | (f) a “collective investment scheme” has the meaning given in regulation 12H of the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015 .
@ref reg 42(2)(f) (src:1344-1344)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 42(2)(f) the meaning of collective investment scheme is given by` MEANS "regulation 12H of the International Tax Compliance Regulations 2015"

-- reg 42(2)(b): a relevant trust.  A record of the facts the three limbs turn on.
DECLARE `reg 42(2)(b) the trust` HAS
    `the trust is an express trust`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust receives income from a source in the United Kingdom`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust has assets in the United Kingdom`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust is liable to pay one or more of the taxes referred to in regulation 45(14) on that income or those assets` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom`                                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the date on which the trustees acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom`               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the last day on which the trustees held that interest`                                           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the trustees enter into a business relationship with a relevant person`                          IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `at least one of the trustees is resident in the United Kingdom`                                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- sub-paragraph (iii)(aaa): "acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest
-- up to and including the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force".  NOTHING for the last day held means the trustees still hold it.
-- src:1333 | (aaa) acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force; or
@ref reg 42(2)(b)(iii)(aaa) (src:1333-1333)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(b) the trust`
      `reg 42(2)(b)(iii)(aaa) the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(2)(b)(iii)(aaa) the trustees acquired an interest in land before 6 October 2020 and continued to hold it up to the commencement date` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `the date on which the trustees acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020" (no acquisition)
    WHEN JUST acquired THEN
        IF acquired LESS THAN Date 6 10 2020 AND `held up to and including the commencement date`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "acquired ... before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force"
    WHERE
        `held up to and including the commencement date` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `the last day on which the trustees held that interest`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST last THEN last AT LEAST `reg 42(2)(b)(iii)(aaa) the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force`

-- SEAM S-18 (asking); SEAM S-K1 and S-8 (asking), answered into the record's business-relationship field by the caller.
-- src:1325 | (b) a “relevant trust” is—
-- src:1326 | (i) a UK trust which is an express trust; ...
-- src:1327 | (ii) a non-UK trust which is an express trust; and
-- src:1328 | (aa) receives income from a source in the United Kingdom; or
-- src:1329 | (bb) has assets in the United Kingdom,
-- src:1330 | on which it is liable to pay one or more of the taxes referred to in regulation 45(14); or
-- src:1331 | (iii) any other non-UK trust which is an express trust, is not a trust listed in Schedule 3A (excluded trusts) and whose trustees (in their capacity as such)—
-- src:1332 | (aa) acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom; ...
-- src:1333 | (aaa) acquired an interest in land in the United Kingdom before 6th October 2020 and continued to hold that interest up to and including the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force; or
-- src:1334 | (bb) enter into a business relationship with a relevant person, where at least one of those trustees is resident in the United Kingdom and the trust is not an EEA registered trust;
@ref reg 42(2)(b) (src:1325-1334)
GIVEN facts IS A `reg 42(2)(b) the trust`
      `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trust is an EEA registered trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(b)(iii)(aaa) the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` MEANS
    `mlr2 either is true` (`mlr2 either is true` `limb (i)` `limb (ii)`) `limb (iii)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a 'relevant trust' is (i) ... (ii) ... or (iii) ..." -- a definition, read like "means"; it is false only when every limb has been answered no
    WHERE
        `an express trust` MEANS `mlr2 the fact stated` (facts's `the trust is an express trust`)
        -- (i) a UK trust which is an express trust
        `limb (i)` MEANS `mlr2 both are true` `an express trust` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust`
        -- (ii) a non-UK trust which is an express trust, and (aa) receives income from a source in the UK or (bb) has assets in the UK, on which it is liable to pay one or more of the taxes
        `limb (ii)` MEANS
            `mlr2 both are true` `an express trust`
                (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust`)
                    (`mlr2 the fact stated` (
                        (facts's `the trust receives income from a source in the United Kingdom` OR facts's `the trust has assets in the United Kingdom`)
                        AND facts's `the trust is liable to pay one or more of the taxes referred to in regulation 45(14) on that income or those assets`)))
        -- (iii) any other non-UK express trust, not listed in Schedule 3A, whose trustees (aa) acquire an interest in land, (aaa) acquired one before 6 October 2020 and held it, or (bb) enter into a business relationship with a relevant person where at least one trustee is resident in the UK and the trust is not an EEA registered trust
        `limb (iii)` MEANS
            `mlr2 both are true` `an express trust`
                (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 42(2)(c) the trust is a UK trust`)
                    (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `sch 3A the trust is a trust listed in Schedule 3A`)
                        (`mlr2 either is true` (facts's `the trustees acquire an interest in land in the United Kingdom`)
                            (`mlr2 either is true` (`reg 42(2)(b)(iii)(aaa) the trustees acquired an interest in land before 6 October 2020 and continued to hold it up to the commencement date` facts `reg 42(2)(b)(iii)(aaa) the date on which this sub-paragraph comes into force`)
                                (`mlr2 both are true` (facts's `the trustees enter into a business relationship with a relevant person`)
                                    (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` (facts's `at least one of the trustees is resident in the United Kingdom`))
                                        (`mlr2 the opposite of` `the trust is an EEA registered trust`)))))))

-- reg 42(1): the Part applies to UK bodies corporate and relevant trusts.  It does not say "only".
-- src:1322 | (1) This Part applies to UK bodies corporate and relevant trusts.
@ref reg 42(1) (src:1322-1322)
GIVEN `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 42(1) this Part applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `mlr2 either is true` `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Part applies to UK bodies corporate and relevant trusts"; the paragraph does not say that it applies to no one else

§§ `Regulation 43 -- Corporate bodies: obligations`

-- reg 43(9): "relevant transaction".  SEAM S-1 (asking).
-- src:1384 | (9) For the purposes of this regulation, a “relevant transaction” means a transaction in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27.
@ref reg 43(9) (src:1384-1384)
GIVEN `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(9) the transaction is a relevant transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant transaction' means a transaction in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulation 27 requires customer due diligence measures has not been answered

-- src:1366 | (1) When a UK body corporate which is not listed on a regulated market enters into a relevant transaction with a relevant person, or forms a business relationship with a relevant person, the body corporate must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with—
-- src:1367 | (a) information identifying—
-- src:1368 | (i) its name, registered number, registered office and principal place of business;
-- src:1369 | (ii) its board of directors, or if there is no board, the members of the equivalent management body;
-- src:1370 | (iii) the senior persons responsible for its operations;
-- src:1371 | (iv) the law to which it is subject;
-- src:1372 | (v) its legal owners;
-- src:1373 | (vi) its beneficial owners; and
-- src:1374 | (b) its articles of association or other governing documents.
@ref reg 43(1) (src:1366-1374)
DECLARE `reg 43(1) item` IS ONE OF
    `reg 43(1)(a)(i) its name, registered number, registered office and principal place`
    `reg 43(1)(a)(ii) its board of directors, or if there is no board, the members`
    `reg 43(1)(a)(iii) the senior persons responsible for its operations`
    `reg 43(1)(a)(iv) the law to which it is subject`
    `reg 43(1)(a)(v) its legal owners`
    `reg 43(1)(a)(vi) its beneficial owners`
    `reg 43(1)(b) its articles of association or other governing documents`
    `reg 43(1) another item`

@ref reg 43(1) (src:1366-1374)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 43(1) item`
`reg 43(1) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 43(1)(a)(i) its name, registered number, registered office and principal place`
    , `reg 43(1)(a)(ii) its board of directors, or if there is no board, the members`
    , `reg 43(1)(a)(iii) the senior persons responsible for its operations`
    , `reg 43(1)(a)(iv) the law to which it is subject`
    , `reg 43(1)(a)(v) its legal owners`
    , `reg 43(1)(a)(vi) its beneficial owners`
    , `reg 43(1)(b) its articles of association or other governing documents`

-- reg 43(1): what a UK body corporate must provide to a relevant person on request.
@ref reg 43(1) (src:1366-1374)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 43(1) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(1) the item must be provided to the relevant person` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(i) its name, registered number, registered office and principal place` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(ii) its board of directors, or if there is no board, the members` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(iii) the senior persons responsible for its operations` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(iv) the law to which it is subject` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(v) its legal owners` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(vi) its beneficial owners` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(b) its articles of association or other governing documents` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "must on request from the relevant person provide the relevant person with"
    WHEN `reg 43(1) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists what is to be provided and does not close the list

@ref reg 43(1) (src:1366-1374)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 43(1) item`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 43(1) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(i) its name, registered number, registered office and principal place` THEN JUST "its name, registered number, registered office and principal place of business"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(ii) its board of directors, or if there is no board, the members` THEN JUST "its board of directors, or if there is no board, the members of the equivalent management body"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(iii) the senior persons responsible for its operations` THEN JUST "the senior persons responsible for its operations"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(iv) the law to which it is subject` THEN JUST "the law to which it is subject"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(v) its legal owners` THEN JUST "its legal owners"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(a)(vi) its beneficial owners` THEN JUST "its beneficial owners"
    WHEN `reg 43(1)(b) its articles of association or other governing documents` THEN JUST "its articles of association or other governing documents"
    WHEN `reg 43(1) another item` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 43(1): the occasions on which the duty arises, and what is to be provided.
-- SEAM S-8, S-1, S-K1 (asking)
@ref reg 43(1) (src:1366-1374)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is listed on a regulated market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate enters into a transaction with the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 43(9) the transaction is a relevant transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate forms a business relationship with the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      item IS A `reg 43(1) item`
      `the relevant person has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(1) the body corporate must on request provide the item to the relevant person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the body corporate is listed on a regulated market`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a UK body corporate which is not listed on a regulated market" -- the limiting words sit in a relative clause, not in the "when" (reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F43-2)
        IF `when clause` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a UK body corporate ... enters into a relevant transaction with a relevant person, or forms a business relationship with a relevant person" ("when" counts as "where": a condition that fails gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `when clause` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN
            (IF `the relevant person has made a request`
             THEN `reg 43(1) the item must be provided to the relevant person` item
             ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on request from the relevant person" -- the paragraph says what is to be provided on request and does not say what is to be provided without one (fork F43-3)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant person, the transaction a relevant transaction or the business relationship a business relationship has not been answered
    WHERE
        `when clause` MEANS
            `mlr2 both are true` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
                (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate`
                    (`mlr2 either is true`
                        (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the body corporate enters into a transaction with the relevant person`) `reg 43(9) the transaction is a relevant transaction`)
                        (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the body corporate forms a business relationship with the relevant person`) `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`)))

-- reg 43(2): owners include the owners of any body corporate or trust above.  "include": other persons are left open.
-- src:1375 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a)(v) and (vi), references to the legal owners and beneficial owners of a UK body corporate include a reference to the legal owners and beneficial owners of any body corporate or trust which is directly or indirectly a legal owner or beneficial owner of that body corporate.
@ref reg 43(2) (src:1375-1375)
GIVEN `the person is a legal owner or a beneficial owner of the UK body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a legal owner or a beneficial owner of a body corporate or trust which is directly or indirectly a legal owner or a beneficial owner of the UK body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(2) the person is within the references to the legal owners and beneficial owners of the UK body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the person is a legal owner or a beneficial owner of the UK body corporate`
       OR `the person is a legal owner or a beneficial owner of a body corporate or trust which is directly or indirectly a legal owner or a beneficial owner of the UK body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to the legal owners and beneficial owners of a UK body corporate include a reference to ..."

-- reg 43(3): when sub-paragraph (1)(a)(vi) does not apply.  SEAM S-K2 (asking), as an aggregate over the individuals.
-- src:1376 | (3) Paragraph (1)(a)(vi) does not apply if no person qualifies as a beneficial owner (within the meaning of regulation 5(1)) of—
-- src:1377 | (a) the UK body corporate; or
-- src:1378 | (b) any body corporate which is directly or indirectly the owner of that UK body corporate.
@ref reg 43(3) (src:1376-1378)
GIVEN `reg 5 and 6 any person qualifies as a beneficial owner of the UK body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 5 and 6 any person qualifies as a beneficial owner of a body corporate which is directly or indirectly the owner of the UK body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(3) paragraph (1)(a)(vi) does not apply` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 5 and 6 any person qualifies as a beneficial owner of the UK body corporate`)
        (`mlr2 the opposite of` `reg 5 and 6 any person qualifies as a beneficial owner of a body corporate which is directly or indirectly the owner of the UK body corporate`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply if no person qualifies as a beneficial owner (within the meaning of regulation 5(1)) of (a) the UK body corporate; or (b) any body corporate which is directly or indirectly the owner of that UK body corporate" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md: a person qualifies as a beneficial owner of either)

-- reg 43(4): the notification of a change, within fourteen days from the day the body corporate becomes aware.
-- SEAM S-K1 (asking)
-- src:1379 | (4) If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the identity of the individuals or information falling within paragraph (1), the UK body corporate referred to in paragraph (1) must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change.
@ref reg 43(4) (src:1379-1379)
GIVEN `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the identity of the individuals or information falling within paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(4) the UK body corporate must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate`
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `there is a change in the identity of the individuals or information falling within paragraph (1)`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the identity of the individuals or information falling within paragraph (1), the UK body corporate ... must notify" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- The last day: "within fourteen days from the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change".  The day of awareness is day 0 (fork F43-1).
-- src:1379 | (4) If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the identity of the individuals or information falling within paragraph (1), the UK body corporate referred to in paragraph (1) must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change.
@ref reg 43(4) (src:1379-1379)
GIVEN `the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 43(4) the last day for the notification` MEANS `the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change` PLUS 14

-- src:1379 | (4) If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the identity of the individuals or information falling within paragraph (1), the UK body corporate referred to in paragraph (1) must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change.
@ref reg 43(4) (src:1379-1379)
GIVEN `the date on which the notification was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(4) the notification was given within fourteen days` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the notification was given` (`reg 43(4) the last day for the notification` `the date on which the body corporate becomes aware of the change`) `the date asked`

DECLARE `reg 43(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 43(4) a UK body corporate`

DECLARE `reg 43(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 43(4) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred`

@ref reg 43(4) (src:1379-1379)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 43(4) party` `reg 43(4) act`
`reg 43(4) a UK body corporate must notify the relevant person within fourteen days` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 43(4) a UK body corporate`
    MUST `reg 43(4) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the UK body corporate did not notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which it became aware of the change"

-- reg 43(5) and (6): information to a law enforcement authority.  SEAM S-15: the authority is `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority`.
-- src:1380 | (5) The UK body corporate must on request provide all or part of the information referred to in paragraph (1) to a law enforcement authority.
@ref reg 43(5) (src:1380-1380)
GIVEN `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by a law enforcement authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(5) the UK body corporate must provide all or part of the information to the law enforcement authority on request` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(a) the body is a UK body corporate` `the request is made by a law enforcement authority`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): passed through from the two answers: the paragraph is addressed to "The UK body corporate" and speaks of a request by "a law enforcement authority"; where either was answered no, the duty is answered no

-- src:1381 | (6) Information requested under paragraph (5), must be provided before the end of such reasonable period as may be specified by the law enforcement authority.
@ref reg 43(6) (src:1381-1381)
GIVEN `the date on which the information was provided` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the period specified by the law enforcement authority` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(6) the information was provided before the end of the period specified by the law enforcement authority` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the information was provided` `the last day of the period specified by the law enforcement authority` `the date asked`

-- reg 43(7) and (8): protection.
-- src:1382 | (7) The provision of information in accordance with this regulation is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 43(7) (src:1382-1382)
GIVEN `the information is provided in accordance with regulation 43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(7) the provision of information is not to be taken to breach a restriction on disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the information is provided in accordance with regulation 43`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provision of information in accordance with this regulation"

-- src:1383 | (8) Where a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with this regulation no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the UK body corporate.
@ref reg 43(8) (src:1383-1383)
GIVEN `a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with regulation 43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 43(8) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the UK body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with regulation 43`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with this regulation no civil liability arises" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); the answer says that the protection of this paragraph is not given, not that liability arises)

§§ `Regulation 44 -- Trustee obligations`

-- reg 44(10): the law enforcement authorities.  SEAM S-15 (answering): the function below is `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority`.
-- src:1404 | (10) For the purposes of this regulation, any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority—
-- src:1405 | (a) the Commissioners;
-- src:1406 | (b) the FCA;
-- src:1407 | (c) the NCA;
-- src:1408 | (d) police forces maintained under section 2 of the Police Act 1996 ;
-- src:1409 | (e) the Police of the Metropolis;
-- src:1410 | (f) the Police for the City of London;
-- src:1411 | (g) the Police Service of Scotland;
-- src:1412 | (h) the Police Service of Northern Ireland;
-- src:1413 | (i) the Serious Fraud Office.
@ref reg 44(10) (src:1404-1413)
DECLARE `reg 44(10) body` IS ONE OF
    `reg 44(10)(a) the Commissioners`
    `reg 44(10)(b) the FCA`
    `reg 44(10)(c) the NCA`
    `reg 44(10)(d) police forces maintained under section 2 of the Police Act 1996`
    `reg 44(10)(e) the Police of the Metropolis`
    `reg 44(10)(f) the Police for the City of London`
    `reg 44(10)(g) the Police Service of Scotland`
    `reg 44(10)(h) the Police Service of Northern Ireland`
    `reg 44(10)(i) the Serious Fraud Office`
    `reg 44(10) another body`

@ref reg 44(10) (src:1404-1413)
GIVETH A LIST OF `reg 44(10) body`
`reg 44(10) the entries listed` MEANS LIST
      `reg 44(10)(a) the Commissioners`
    , `reg 44(10)(b) the FCA`
    , `reg 44(10)(c) the NCA`
    , `reg 44(10)(d) police forces maintained under section 2 of the Police Act 1996`
    , `reg 44(10)(e) the Police of the Metropolis`
    , `reg 44(10)(f) the Police for the City of London`
    , `reg 44(10)(g) the Police Service of Scotland`
    , `reg 44(10)(h) the Police Service of Northern Ireland`
    , `reg 44(10)(i) the Serious Fraud Office`

-- reg 44(10): the nine bodies the paragraph lists as law enforcement authorities.
@ref reg 44(10) (src:1404-1413)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 44(10) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(a) the Commissioners` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(b) the FCA` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(c) the NCA` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(d) police forces maintained under section 2 of the Police Act 1996` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(e) the Police of the Metropolis` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(f) the Police for the City of London` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(g) the Police Service of Scotland` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(h) the Police Service of Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(i) the Serious Fraud Office` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"
    WHEN `reg 44(10) another body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3 gives "law enforcement authority" the meaning in regulation 44(10): "For the purposes of this regulation, any of the following authorities is a law enforcement authority"; a body in none of the heads is not one (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated definitions (a))

@ref reg 44(10) (src:1404-1413)
GIVEN item IS A `reg 44(10) body`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`reg 44(10) the wording of the entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(a) the Commissioners` THEN JUST "the Commissioners"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(b) the FCA` THEN JUST "the FCA"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(c) the NCA` THEN JUST "the NCA"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(d) police forces maintained under section 2 of the Police Act 1996` THEN JUST "police forces maintained under section 2 of the Police Act 1996"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(e) the Police of the Metropolis` THEN JUST "the Police of the Metropolis"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(f) the Police for the City of London` THEN JUST "the Police for the City of London"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(g) the Police Service of Scotland` THEN JUST "the Police Service of Scotland"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(h) the Police Service of Northern Ireland` THEN JUST "the Police Service of Northern Ireland"
    WHEN `reg 44(10)(i) the Serious Fraud Office` THEN JUST "the Serious Fraud Office"
    WHEN `reg 44(10) another body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives no wording for a case it does not list

-- reg 44(10), the same question about the core's own `Authority` values, for the bodies of the list that the core names.
@ref reg 44(10) (src:1404-1413)
GIVEN authority IS AN Authority
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(10) the authority is a law enforcement authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER authority
    WHEN `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "(a) the Commissioners"
    WHEN `the Financial Conduct Authority` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "(b) the FCA"
    WHEN `the National Crime Agency` THEN JUST TRUE -- listed: "(c) the NCA"
    WHEN `the Prudential Regulation Authority` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3 gives "law enforcement authority" the meaning in regulation 44(10), which lists nine bodies; this body is in none of them (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05)
    WHEN `the Gambling Commission` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3 gives "law enforcement authority" the meaning in regulation 44(10), which lists nine bodies; this body is in none of them (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05)
    WHEN `the Treasury` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3 gives "law enforcement authority" the meaning in regulation 44(10), which lists nine bodies; this body is in none of them (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05)
    WHEN `the Department for the Economy in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3 gives "law enforcement authority" the meaning in regulation 44(10), which lists nine bodies; this body is in none of them (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05)
    WHEN `a local weights and measures authority` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3 gives "law enforcement authority" the meaning in regulation 44(10), which lists nine bodies; this body is in none of them (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05)
    WHEN `a professional body listed in Schedule 1` body THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): regulation 3 gives "law enforcement authority" the meaning in regulation 44(10), which lists nine bodies; a professional body is in none of them (a definition the text hands to a list, ruling of 2026-11-05)

-- reg 44(1)
-- src:1386 | (1) The trustees of a relevant trust must maintain accurate and up-to-date records in writing of all the beneficial owners of the trust, and of any potential beneficiaries referred to in paragraph (5)(b), containing the information required by regulation 45(2)(b) to (d) and (5)(f) and (g).
@ref reg 44(1) (src:1386-1386)
GIVEN `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(1) the trustees of the relevant trust must maintain accurate and up-to-date records in writing of all the beneficial owners of the trust and of any potential beneficiaries` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustees of a relevant trust must"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the trust is a relevant trust has not been answered

-- A compliance check, in the reading of marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md: an undischarged "must" is a "no".
-- src:1386 | (1) The trustees of a relevant trust must maintain accurate and up-to-date records in writing of all the beneficial owners of the trust, and of any potential beneficiaries referred to in paragraph (5)(b), containing the information required by regulation 45(2)(b) to (d) and (5)(f) and (g).
@ref reg 44(1) (src:1386-1386)
GIVEN `the records are accurate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are up-to-date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records contain the information required by regulation 45(2)(b) to (d) and (5)(f) and (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(1) the trustees have maintained the records` MEANS
    IF `the records are accurate` AND `the records are up-to-date` AND `the records are in writing` AND `the records contain the information required by regulation 45(2)(b) to (d) and (5)(f) and (g)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must maintain accurate and up-to-date records in writing ... containing the information required by regulation 45(2)(b) to (d) and (5)(f) and (g)" (a "must" not discharged, marginal reading (c) of NOTES.md)

-- reg 44(4): "relevant transaction".  SEAM S-1 (asking).
-- src:1391 | (4) For the purposes of this regulation, a “relevant transaction” means a transaction in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27.
@ref reg 44(4) (src:1391-1391)
GIVEN `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(4) the transaction is a relevant transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 27 the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant transaction' means a transaction in relation to which the relevant person is required to apply customer due diligence measures under regulation 27"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulation 27 requires customer due diligence measures has not been answered

-- reg 44(2): the occasions on which the trustee must inform and provide.
-- SEAM S-8, S-1, S-K1 (asking)
-- src:1387 | (2) When a trustee of a relevant trust, acting as trustee, enters into a relevant transaction with a relevant person, or forms a business relationship with a relevant person, the trustee must—
-- src:1388 | (a) inform the relevant person that it is acting as trustee; and
-- src:1389 | (b) on request from the relevant person, provide the relevant person with information identifying all the beneficial owners of the trust (which, in the case of a class of beneficiaries, may be done by describing the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust).
@ref reg 44(2) (src:1387-1389)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustee is acting as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee enters into a transaction with the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 44(4) the transaction is a relevant transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustee forms a business relationship with the relevant person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(2) the trustee enters into a relevant transaction or forms a business relationship with a relevant person` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person`
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust`
            (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the trustee is acting as trustee`)
                (`mlr2 either is true`
                    (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the trustee enters into a transaction with the relevant person`) `reg 44(4) the transaction is a relevant transaction`)
                    (`mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the trustee forms a business relationship with the relevant person`) `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship`))))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): passed through from the answers it is made of; the occasions are those of "When a trustee of a relevant trust, acting as trustee, enters into a relevant transaction with a relevant person, or forms a business relationship with a relevant person"

-- src:1387 | (2) When a trustee of a relevant trust, acting as trustee, enters into a relevant transaction with a relevant person, or forms a business relationship with a relevant person, the trustee must—
-- src:1388 | (a) inform the relevant person that it is acting as trustee; and
@ref reg 44(2)(a) (src:1387-1388)
GIVEN `reg 44(2) the trustee enters into a relevant transaction or forms a business relationship with a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(2)(a) the trustee must inform the relevant person that it is acting as trustee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 44(2) the trustee enters into a relevant transaction or forms a business relationship with a relevant person`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a trustee of a relevant trust, acting as trustee, enters into a relevant transaction with a relevant person, or forms a business relationship" ("when" counts as "where": a condition that fails gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer the duty depends on has not been given

-- src:1387 | (2) When a trustee of a relevant trust, acting as trustee, enters into a relevant transaction with a relevant person, or forms a business relationship with a relevant person, the trustee must—
-- src:1388 | (a) inform the relevant person that it is acting as trustee; and
-- src:1389 | (b) on request from the relevant person, provide the relevant person with information identifying all the beneficial owners of the trust (which, in the case of a class of beneficiaries, may be done by describing the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust).
@ref reg 44(2)(b) (src:1387-1389)
GIVEN `reg 44(2) the trustee enters into a relevant transaction or forms a business relationship with a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person has requested the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(2)(b) the trustee must provide the relevant person with information identifying all the beneficial owners of the trust` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 44(2) the trustee enters into a relevant transaction or forms a business relationship with a relevant person`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the relevant person has requested the information`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on request from the relevant person"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When a trustee of a relevant trust, acting as trustee, enters into a relevant transaction ... or forms a business relationship" ("when" counts as "where": a condition that fails gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer the duty depends on has not been given

-- reg 44(2)(b), in brackets: for a class of beneficiaries the information "may be done by describing the class".
-- src:1389 | (b) on request from the relevant person, provide the relevant person with information identifying all the beneficial owners of the trust (which, in the case of a class of beneficiaries, may be done by describing the class of persons who are beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries under the trust).
@ref reg 44(2)(b) (src:1389-1389)
GIVEN `the beneficiaries or potential beneficiaries are a class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
