    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a class of beneficiaries"

-- reg 44(3): the notification of a change, within fourteen days from the day any one of the trustees became aware.
-- src:1390 | (3) If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the information provided under paragraph (2), the trustees must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change.
@ref reg 44(3) (src:1390-1390)
GIVEN `the relevant person was provided with information under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `there is a change in the information provided under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(3) the trustees must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the relevant person was provided with information under paragraph (2)`)
        (`mlr2 both are true` `reg 4(1) to (3) there is a business relationship` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `there is a change in the information provided under paragraph (2)`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the information provided under paragraph (2), the trustees must notify" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a) of NOTES.md)

-- src:1390 | (3) If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the information provided under paragraph (2), the trustees must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change.
@ref reg 44(3) (src:1390-1390)
GIVEN `the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 44(3) the last day for the notification` MEANS `the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change` PLUS 14

-- src:1390 | (3) If, during the course of a business relationship, there is any change in the information provided under paragraph (2), the trustees must notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change.
@ref reg 44(3) (src:1390-1390)
GIVEN `the date on which the notification was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(3) the notification was given within fourteen days` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the notification was given` (`reg 44(3) the last day for the notification` `the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change`) `the date asked`

DECLARE `reg 44(3) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 44(3) the trustees of a relevant trust`

DECLARE `reg 44(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 44(3) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred`

@ref reg 44(3) (src:1390-1390)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 44(3) party` `reg 44(3) act`
`reg 44(3) the trustees must notify the relevant person within fourteen days` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 44(3) the trustees of a relevant trust`
    MUST `reg 44(3) notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the trustees did not notify the relevant person of the change and the date on which it occurred within fourteen days from the date on which any one of the trustees became aware of the change"

-- reg 44(5) and (6): information to a law enforcement authority.  SEAM S-15: the authority is `reg 44(10) the body is a law enforcement authority`.
DECLARE `reg 44(5) matter` IS ONE OF
    `reg 44(5)(a) the beneficial owners of the trust`
    `reg 44(5)(b) any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes`
    `reg 44(5) another matter`

-- src:1392 | (5) The trustees of a relevant trust must on request provide information to any law enforcement authority—
-- src:1393 | (a) about the beneficial owners of the trust; and
-- src:1394 | (b) about any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes.
@ref reg 44(5) (src:1392-1394)
GIVEN `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by a law enforcement authority` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `reg 44(5) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(5) the trustees must on request provide the information to the law enforcement authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `mlr2 both are true` `reg 42(2)(b) the trust is a relevant trust` `the request is made by a law enforcement authority`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `reg 44(5)(a) the beneficial owners of the trust` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 44(5)(b) any other individual referred to as a potential beneficiary in a document from the settlor relating to the trust such as a letter of wishes` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `reg 44(5) another matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph lists (a) and (b) and does not say that nothing else is to be provided
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): passed through: "The trustees of a relevant trust must on request provide information to any law enforcement authority" -- a no from either answer is a no here
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer the duty depends on has not been given

-- src:1395 | (6) Information requested under paragraph (5) must be provided before the end of such reasonable period as may be specified by the law enforcement authority.
@ref reg 44(6) (src:1395-1395)
GIVEN `the date on which the information was provided` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the period specified by the law enforcement authority` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(6) the information was provided before the end of the period specified by the law enforcement authority` MEANS
    `mlr2 the event was on or before the last day, asked on a day` `the date on which the information was provided` `the last day of the period specified by the law enforcement authority` `the date asked`

-- reg 44(7) and (8): protection.
-- src:1396 | (7) The provision of information in accordance with this regulation is not to be taken to breach any restriction, however imposed, on the disclosure of information.
@ref reg 44(7) (src:1396-1396)
GIVEN `the information is provided in accordance with regulation 44` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(7) the provision of information is not to be taken to breach a restriction on disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the information is provided in accordance with regulation 44`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provision of information in accordance with this regulation"

-- src:1397 | (8) Where a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with this regulation no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the trustees of a relevant trust.
@ref reg 44(8) (src:1397-1397)
GIVEN `a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with regulation 44` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(8) no civil liability arises in respect of the disclosure on the part of the trustees` MEANS
    IF `a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with regulation 44`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure is made in good faith in accordance with this regulation no civil liability arises" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); the answer says that the protection of this paragraph is not given, not that liability arises)

-- reg 44(9): trustees who are paid and are relevant persons.  The whole of "If the trustees of a relevant trust are relevant persons who are being paid to act as trustees of that trust" is the condition ("if": an unmet condition gives no, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).
-- SEAM S-8 (asking)
-- src:1398 | (9) If the trustees of a relevant trust are relevant persons who are being paid to act as trustees of that trust, they must—
-- src:1399 | (a) retain the records referred to in paragraph (1) for a period of five years after the date on which the final distribution is made under the trust;
-- src:1400 | (b) make arrangements for those records to be deleted at the end of that period, unless—
-- src:1401 | (i) the trustees are required to retain them by or under any enactment or for the purpose of court proceedings;
-- src:1402 | (ii) any person to whom information in a record relates consents to the retention of that information; or
-- src:1403 | (iii) the trustees have reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings.
@ref reg 44(9) (src:1398-1403)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(9)(a) the trustees must retain the records for a period of five years after the date on which the final distribution is made` MEANS
    `reg 44(9) the condition holds` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the trustees of a relevant trust are relevant persons who are being paid to act as trustees of that trust" -- the answer is no where the trustees are not paid, or are not relevant persons (an "if" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05)

-- The condition of regulation 44(9), shared by (a) and (b).
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(9) the condition holds` MEANS
    `mlr2 both are true` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` (`mlr2 the fact stated` `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust`)

-- "a period of five years after the date": the fifth anniversary of the day of the final distribution is the last day of the period (fork F44-1).
-- src:1399 | (a) retain the records referred to in paragraph (1) for a period of five years after the date on which the final distribution is made under the trust;
@ref reg 44(9)(a) (src:1399-1399)
GIVEN `the date on which the final distribution is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 44(9)(a) the last day of the period of five years after the final distribution` MEANS `add years` `the date on which the final distribution is made` 5

-- The same period asked on a day: "must the trustees still retain the records on 1 June?"  A MAYBE DATE: NOTHING means the final distribution has not been made.
-- src:1399 | (a) retain the records referred to in paragraph (1) for a period of five years after the date on which the final distribution is made under the trust;
@ref reg 44(9)(a) (src:1399-1399)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the final distribution is made` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(9)(a) the trustees must still retain the records on the date asked` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 44(9) the condition holds` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the trustees of a relevant trust are relevant persons who are being paid to act as trustees of that trust" (an "if" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05)
        IF `reg 44(9) the condition holds` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant person is regulation 8's answer and has not been given
        OTHERWISE
            (CONSIDER `the date on which the final distribution is made`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the final distribution has not been made, so the period of five years has not begun
             WHEN JUST distribution THEN
                 IF `the date asked` GREATER THAN distribution AND `the date asked` AT MOST `reg 44(9)(a) the last day of the period of five years after the final distribution` distribution
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of five years after the date on which the final distribution is made" -- a period the text fixes in its own words; a day on or before the distribution, or after the last day, is outside it (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a); fork F44-1)

-- src:1400 | (b) make arrangements for those records to be deleted at the end of that period, unless—
-- src:1401 | (i) the trustees are required to retain them by or under any enactment or for the purpose of court proceedings;
-- src:1402 | (ii) any person to whom information in a record relates consents to the retention of that information; or
-- src:1403 | (iii) the trustees have reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings.
@ref reg 44(9)(b) (src:1400-1403)
GIVEN `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees are required to retain the records by or under any enactment or for the purpose of court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person to whom information in a record relates consents to the retention of that information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustees have reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(9)(b) the trustees must make arrangements for the records to be deleted at the end of that period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 44(9) the condition holds` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the trustees of a relevant trust are relevant persons who are being paid to act as trustees of that trust" (an "if" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05)
        IF `reg 44(9) the condition holds` `reg 8 the person is a relevant person` `the trustees are being paid to act as trustees of the trust` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a relevant person is regulation 8's answer and has not been given
        IF `the trustees are required to retain the records by or under any enactment or for the purpose of court proceedings`
           OR `a person to whom information in a record relates consents to the retention of that information`
           OR `the trustees have reasonable grounds for believing that records containing the personal data need to be retained for the purpose of legal proceedings`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make arrangements for those records to be deleted at the end of that period, unless" (i), (ii) or (iii)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- reg 44(11): collective investment schemes.  "includes": other persons are left open.
-- src:1414 | (11) For the purposes of this regulation, in the case of a relevant trust which is a collective investment scheme, a reference to the trustees of a relevant trust includes a reference to the manager or operator of the collective investment scheme.
@ref reg 44(11) (src:1414-1414)
GIVEN `the relevant trust is a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee of the relevant trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the manager or operator of the collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 44(11) the person is within the reference to the trustees of the relevant trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a trustee of the relevant trust` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the relevant trust is a collective investment scheme` AND `the person is the manager or operator of the collective investment scheme` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to the trustees of a relevant trust includes a reference to the manager or operator of the collective investment scheme"
